// ============================================================================
// HUB - SHIFT START (Supervisor board)
//
// Flow (tabs, left to right):
//   1. Teams     – shift is detected automatically; pick leads, drag employees under them.
//                  Overtime: pull in someone from another crew. "Out" zone for PTO / Sick / Late.
//   2. Lines     – pick which lines are down for cleaning (manual until the production
//                  scheduler drives it), add manual tasks, drop teams onto lines.
//                  Production lines sort above non-production lines.
//   3. Equipment – each line's equipment is split across the people on it automatically;
//                  drag equipment between people (or people between lines) to adjust.
//   4. Manage    – progress per line, then the shift update: copy/paste or Send to Teams.
//                  Once the board is set up, the app opens on this tab.
//
// Dataverse
//   craa5__aa_employee          roster (craa5_role: 256000001 lead, 256000002 supervisor, 256000003 manager)
//   craa5_aa_mss_area           lines (craa5_production, craa5_everyday)
//   craa5_aa_assets             equipment (craa5_areaname -> line)
//   craa5_workshift             crew rotation (same parser as Ganttly)
//   craa5_taskassignment        one open row per person on the board (what Gantt / Manager read).
//                               Moving someone closes their row (craa5_endtime) and opens a new one.
//   craa5_sanitationshiftreport "Board · …"        whole board, so a reload or another device picks up where you left off
//                               "Teams Update · …" one row per update sent to Teams
//
// Teams posting (one-time Power Automate setup)
//   Trigger: Dataverse "When a row is added" on craa5_sanitationshiftreport,
//            filter rows: startswith(craa5_name, 'Teams Update')
//   Action:  Teams "Post message in a chat or channel", message = craa5_handofftext.
//   The app writes those rows from "Send to Teams" and, with auto-send on, at
//   3, 9 and 12 AM/PM while it is open.
// ============================================================================

